## What your app is missing most

Your current app already has bots, puzzles, micro-lessons, model games, progress stages, daily goals and a family section. I couldn’t find public-facing evidence yet of personalised game review, multiplayer, varied puzzle modes, opening repetition, bot personalities, quests, cosmetics or detailed family reports. ([Chess Kappa Five][1])

The strongest ideas used elsewhere are:

* **Chess.com:** personality bots, lessons, Puzzle Rush/Battle, analysis, game review and odds chess. ([Chess.com][2])
* **Lichess:** Puzzle Streak/Storm/Racer, variants, studies, tournaments and extensive analysis. ([lichess.org][3])
* **ChessKid:** quests, animated characters, coins, stars, avatar items and child-focused progression. The standalone Adventure app is no longer officially supported, but its ideas remain excellent. ([ChessKid Help Center][4])
* **Shredder:** automatic difficulty adjustment, estimated Elo, mistake warnings and different engine personalities. ([Shredder Chess][5])
* **Magnus Trainer, Chessable and Duolingo:** mini-games, bite-sized learning, spaced repetition, XP and mini-matches. ([App Store][6])

