# How the vibe-coding workflow should operate

For each feature, give the coding agent **one ticket only**:

1. Inspect the current implementation.
2. List the existing files involved.
3. Explain the smallest architecture change required.
4. Add a feature flag.
5. Add the database migration.
6. Implement the server logic.
7. Implement the UI.
8. Add tests.
9. Run lint, type-check and production build.
10. Test existing play, puzzle, login and mobile behaviour.
11. Commit that single feature.

A ticket is not done merely because the page renders. It must survive refreshes, mobile screens, login/logout, invalid requests and repeat attempts.

The best next move is **Merciful Puzzle Mode plus persistent puzzle attempts**. It solves the frustration you already experienced and creates the puzzle state system needed by Rush, Streak, Daily Dungeon, family duels and several mini-games.

